"comparison": "Both BAC and JPM disclose total estimated uninsured deposits at year-end 2024, showing a similar upward trend. BAC reported $646.2 billion in U.S. and $124.9 billion in non-U.S. uninsured deposits (totaling ~$771.1 billion) at Dec 31, 2024, compared to $606.8 billion and $116.6 billion in 2023. JPM reported total estimated uninsured deposits of $1,414.0 billion at Dec 31, 2024, up from $1,347.8 billion in 2023. JPM specifies that its uninsured deposits are primarily wholesale operating deposits and that non-U.S. time deposits are deemed uninsured, whereas BAC explicitly excludes derivative collateral and accrued interest from its estimates.",
